# Flutter API Client Rules

- API contracts come from `/laravel/docs/api.md` and shared use cases.
- Use typed request/response models for non-trivial endpoints.
- Centralize authentication headers, base URL, timeout, serialization, and common error mapping.
- Never trust server response data without parsing/validation.
- Never send authoritative financial values simply because the UI calculated them.
- Commands that may be retried must carry the required idempotency/event identifier.
- Handle HTTP errors, timeouts, connectivity failures, authentication expiry, and validation errors distinctly.
- Do not mix raw HTTP calls directly into presentation widgets.
